Call the lock-selected distributions (psycopg 3, pgspecial, cli_helpers, tabulate, sqlparse, prompt_toolkit, pygments, click, configobj, keyring, sshtunnel, tzlocal, setproctitle) directly; no Cott facade or binding wraps them.
Implementations may not define classes, nested functions, decorators, global/nonlocal statements or mutable module globals: keep state that callbacks change in local one-element lists (cells) created by the canonical function. A private helper may only appear as an exact call, never as a value (no functools.partial(_helper, ...), no target=_helper, no passing _helper to register): wrap it in a lambda that calls it, for example kb.add("f2")(lambda event: _on_f2(cells, event)) or special.register(lambda *args, **kwargs: _pgcli_command_handler(), ...).
A prompt_toolkit completer without subclassing is typing.cast(prompt_toolkit.completion.Completer, types.SimpleNamespace(get_completions=lambda document, complete_event: _complete(cells, document, complete_event))) wrapped in prompt_toolkit.completion.ThreadedCompleter; ThreadedCompleter only calls get_completions(document, complete_event) on the wrapped object.
Untyped distributions (pgspecial, cli_helpers, configobj, sshtunnel, tabulate): bind their objects to names annotated typing.Any (for example special: Any = PGSpecial()) and convert every value read from them with cast(object, ...) followed by isinstance checks, or str()/int()/bool() of a narrowed value, before it reaches typed code; never leave Unknown types.
Opaque handles: build them with cott_runtime.Opaque(tag="<the alias tag>", value=obj) and read them with cast(<concrete type>, handle.unwrap()); the psycopg connection type is psycopg.Connection[tuple[object, ...]].
BasedPyright narrowing: iterate CottList values directly; narrow Option with isinstance(value, Some) and treat the else branch as Nothing; handle the last variant of a closed enum union in a final else without another isinstance test; do not isinstance-test a value whose static type already guarantees it.
psycopg typing: build libpq conninfo with psycopg.conninfo.make_conninfo and pass it positionally to psycopg.connect; never expand a dict into psycopg.connect's keyword parameters. conninfo_to_dict returns values typed str | int | None: narrow each. Pass user-authored SQL to Cursor.execute encoded as UTF-8 bytes or wrapped with psycopg.sql.SQL; keep fixed SQL as LiteralString literals and compose identifiers with psycopg.sql.Identifier. isinstance(value, memoryview) yields memoryview[Unknown]; cast(memoryview[int], value) before bytes(value).
JSON typing: json.loads returns Any; after an isinstance list or dict test cast to list[object] or dict[object, object] before use and check every element.
subprocess typing: annotate text-mode processes as subprocess.Popen[str] and subprocess.CompletedProcess[str]; stream helper parameters are typing.IO[str].
Error helpers return the declared error union type (for example Err[<ErrorEnum>]), not a variant-specific Err. Path values are pathlib.Path.
Terminal output goes through click.echo / click.secho exactly as the contract says (they strip ANSI escapes when the stream is not a terminal); never print passwords.
cott-domain real.pgcli.cli.run return: annotate the return type as typing.Never exactly, not typing.NoReturn; the signature is def run(arguments: CottList[str]) -> Never.
